C.  HONEST TWO-SIDED BRACKET.  The linear EFE response tensor has eigenvalues nu_e*(1+L_e) along g_e
    and nu_e transverse.  ANY orientation weighting lies between them.  FM12 1-D = the ALONG eigenvalue
    (the SMALLEST prediction -> LARGEST residual).  The transverse eigenvalue is the opposite edge.
    The exact isotropic (sphere) average nu_e*(1+L_e/3) sits strictly between.  So:
    FM12 1-D  (ALONG edge, smallest prediction)    matched separation +0.1569 dex  (N=14)
    sphere average (exact isotropic)               matched separation +0.0644 dex  (N=14)
    transverse edge (largest prediction)           matched separation +0.0647 dex  (N=14)

    -> the FULL physically-allowed orientation bracket does not contain zero and never changes sign.

